which is "normal", and "battle"\par
however, you can set a direction flag in there\par
i believe it is 0x20\par
then there is a direction you can assign\par
offset 0x00: Flag\{Byte\} - CAM Attributes \{1: Normal, 2: Battle, 4: Event, 8: Door, 16: Once, 32: Ahead, 64: Direct, 128: Dislgt (Disregard light?)\} Note If "Door" is enabled "Ahead" must also be enabled; If "Event" is enabled nothing else can be enabled\par
I'm not sure what all of them do yet\par
but in the Area Properties (the first of the two offsets) there is \par
offset 0x04: Float Direction - When CAM Attributes are set to direction, this it the facing. (in radians [-3.14 - 3.14])\par
It's in radians relative to the Y axis I thing\par
\par
so these are the CAM attributes\par

